Z||000000||JetroGT||10-05-2001||12:56 AM||||I made this diagram for thoughs of us who like a visiual aid. <BR>The two pink wires are from the Amplifier/Filter. Cut one and run it to your red ingnition power. Connect the blue wire from your aftermarket radio to pin 8.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AfterMarketRadioDiagram1.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||10-05-2001||10:08 AM||||Hey Jetro, aren't you suppose to connect both pink wires to the ignition?<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011151.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011151.html</A> <P>That's how I did my and it works fine.  By the way where does the other pink wire connect to?||||reg||1
Z||000002||86seyellow||10-05-2001||10:14 AM||||correct, the opther pink wire is grounded already for what I know. I put all new system in a year ago witha 10" sub. USed existing wires and did as diagram says. Perfect except now you have to check all screws case they get loose from the bass<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1_copy1.jpg">    <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86seyellow_01.jpg">  <P>I can go as fast as I want unless I get caught||||reg||1
